<title>FINLAND: Silja channel rationlisation to up result.</title>
<headline>Silja channel rationlisation to up result.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1996-09-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finnish passenger ferry operator Silja Oy said in a statement on Friday it was transferring its English channel traffic to a new company, Holyman Sally, of which it owns one third.</p>
<p>&quot;As a result of the arrangement, Sally UK's result will improve significantly from spring 1997,&quot; it said.</p>
<p>Australian shipping company Holyman owns the two thirds majority of Holyman Sally.</p>
</text>
